---
// The Vancouver time-and-weather example: two model API calls, with both tools run in parallel between them (redraw of Fig 2-3).
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 552"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d2-tcs-title d2-tcs-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d2-tcs-title">Complete interaction sequence for two model API calls</title>
	<desc id="d2-tcs-desc">
		First model API call: the request carries the system and user messages plus the tools get_current_time and
		get_weather. Through the API, the model returns an assistant message with tool_calls:
		get_current_time(timezone="America/Vancouver") and get_weather(city="Vancouver", unit="celsius"). The two have no
		data dependency, so they can run in parallel, and the agent framework executes the two tools in parallel. Second
		model API call: the messages now add the tool results, Vancouver time and weather, appended to the message
		history before requesting the model again. Through the API, the model returns the assistant's final reply, "Now
		it is…, and the weather is…". There is no tool call, so the loop ends. With a stateless API, the complete message
		history must be resent to the model in every round.
	</desc>
	<defs>
		<marker id="d2-tcs-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
			<path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="dg-arrowhead"></path>
		</marker>
	</defs>

	<text x="2" y="28" class="dg-title">Complete interaction sequence for two model API calls</text>

	<text x="6" y="66" font-weight="700">First model API call</text>

	<!-- 1. First call -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-context" data-step="1" data-step-label="API call 1 sends the system and user messages plus the tool definitions">
		<rect x="6" y="80" width="270" height="110" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="141" y="110" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">messages: system + user</text>
		<text x="141" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">tools: get_current_time,</text>
		<text x="141" y="162" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">get_weather</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-edge" data-step="1">
		<line x1="276" y1="135" x2="336" y2="135" marker-end="url(#d2-tcs-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="306" y="125" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">API</text>
	</g>

	<!-- 2. tool_calls -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-model" data-step="2" data-step-label="The model returns two tool_calls with no data dependency" style="font-variant-ligatures: none">
		<rect x="338" y="80" width="376" height="158" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="526" y="106" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">assistant: tool_calls</text>
		<text x="354" y="132" class="dg-mono">get_current_time(</text>
		<text x="374" y="154" class="dg-mono">timezone="America/Vancouver")</text>
		<text x="354" y="176" class="dg-mono">get_weather(city="Vancouver",</text>
		<text x="374" y="198" class="dg-mono">unit="celsius")</text>
		<text x="526" y="224" text-anchor="middle">No data dependency → can run in parallel</text>
	</g>

	<!-- 3. Parallel execution -->
	<g class="dg-edge" data-step="3">
		<line x1="526" y1="238" x2="526" y2="266" marker-end="url(#d2-tcs-arrow)"></line>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-harness" data-step="3" data-step-label="The agent framework executes both tools in parallel">
		<rect x="338" y="268" width="376" height="70" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="526" y="297" text-anchor="middle">Agent framework executes</text>
		<text x="526" y="321" text-anchor="middle">two tools in parallel</text>
	</g>

	<text x="6" y="354" font-weight="700">Second model API call</text>

	<!-- 4. Append results -->
	<g class="dg-edge" data-step="4">
		<line x1="526" y1="338" x2="526" y2="366" marker-end="url(#d2-tcs-arrow)"></line>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-context" data-step="4" data-step-label="The tool results are appended to the message history">
		<rect x="338" y="368" width="376" height="110" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="526" y="394" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">messages: + tool results</text>
		<text x="526" y="418" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">Vancouver time &amp; weather</text>
		<text x="526" y="442" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">Append to message history,</text>
		<text x="526" y="464" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">then request model again</text>
	</g>

	<!-- 5. Final reply -->
	<g class="dg-edge" data-step="5">
		<line x1="338" y1="423" x2="278" y2="423" marker-end="url(#d2-tcs-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="308" y="413" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-edge-label">API</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-model" data-step="5" data-step-label="API call 2 returns a final reply with no tool call, so the loop ends">
		<rect x="6" y="368" width="270" height="110" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="141" y="398" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">assistant: final reply</text>
		<text x="141" y="424" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">No tool call → end loop</text>
		<text x="141" y="450" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">"Now it is…, and the weather is…"</text>
	</g>

	<text x="360" y="516" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">With a stateless API, the complete message history</text>
	<text x="360" y="538" text-anchor="middle" class="dg-sub">must be resent to the model in every round</text>
</svg>
